' Source: src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx — the header theme toggle
' The accessible name and the icon BOTH name the DESTINATION, not the current
' state. So in light mode you see a Moon; in dark you see a Sun. Icon and label
' always agree with each other, and both disagree with the theme you are in.
' A rubric expecting "dark mode shows a moon" asserts the opposite of the design.
'
' Zoom (⌘+ / ⌘- / ⌘0) has NO visible control — nothing here changes. It rescales
' every capture instead. Reset it to 1 before screenshotting anything.
@startsalt
{
  {#
    <b>theme | <b>icon | <b>accessible name        | <b>on click
    light    | 🌙     | "Switch to dark theme"     | -> dark
    dark     | ☀      | "Switch to light theme"    | -> light
  }
  ==
  <b>Header order, left to right
  {+
    { [☰] | 📄 Getting started > 📄 Notes | . | (☁/ Local only) | [🌙] | [⬇] | [☆] | [Sign in to sync] }
  }
  --
  <i>Both this toggle and Settings' Light/Dark pair write the same
  <i>`workspace-v1` theme field. Two controls, one piece of state.
  <i>useTheme() in __root.tsx applies `.dark`, so /login is themed too even
  <i>though this header never renders there.
}
@endsalt
